(A1 — global list growth inside a function must keep the reallocated list
 pointer in the global BSS mirror so a later direct use sees the new length.)

a list called items is [].

To 'grow'.
  a number called i is 1.
  While i is less than or equal to 100,
    append i to items,
    increment i.


To 'check'.
  If items's length is equal to 100, print "ok". Otherwise, print "bad".


'grow'.
'check'.
